. * ---- a two-mode network: 30 people by 12 clubs (simulated for this tutorial)
. clear

. set seed 20261024

. nwclear

. mata:
------------------------------------------------- mata (type end to exit) -----------------------------------------------
: g1 = (runiform(30,1) :> 0.5) :+ 1

: g2 = (runiform(12,1) :> 0.5) :+ 1

: P = J(30,12,0.08)

: for (i=1;i<=30;i++) for (j=1;j<=12;j++) if (g1[i]==g2[j]) P[i,j] = 0.30
> B = (runiform(30,12) :< P)

: st_matrix("B", B')

: end
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. nwset, mat(B) bipartite name(clubs)

. set obs 42
Number of observations (_N) was 42, now 42.

. generate byte kind = .
(42 missing values generated)

. mata: st_store(., "kind", (g1 \ g2))

. nwsummarize
--------------------------------------------------
   Network name:  clubs
   Network id:  1
   Directed: false
   Valued: false
   Two-mode: true
   Nodes: 42
      Level 1: 30 ()
      Level 2: 12 ()
   Selfloop: false
   Edges: 71
   Minimum value:  0
   Maximum value:  1
   Density:  .197
   Temporal: false

. nwergm clubs, edges nodemix(kind)

